 "logline": "A fire alarm at three in the morning, a chastity talk with a slideshow, a beach cleanup that is absolutely not a date — and after a barn party, Lena asks to be walked home the long way.",
 "previously": [
  {
   "text": "At Sully’s, Lena painted a gold fleur-de-lis on your cheekbone. “It means home, Costigan. It means we came back.”",
   "if": "e5_paint==\"meaning\""
  },
  {
   "text": "Hale asked whether luck can make a man guilty. You said the unlucky driver owes everything — that nobody gets to take it for him.",
   "if": "e5_ferocity"
  },
  {
   "text": "A girl in Gina’s religion class called her the class expert on visiting the imprisoned. Lena said: tell her to say his name.",
   "if": "e5_gina_lena"
  },
  {
   "text": "Laney got Pi Lam. She ran back across Seacliff to Lena first."
  },
  {
   "text": "On the bluff bench your brother called from Trumbull, and Lena said hi to him. Then the system cut him off: “Tell Gina — .”",
   "if": "danny_met_lena"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your brother called from Trumbull. Then the system cut him off: “Tell Gina — .”",
   "if": "!danny_met_lena"
  },
  {
   "text": "At 2:14 a.m.: “Sixty-one. No second engine tonight. Goodnight, Jack.”"
